@page "/privacy"
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}
<h1>Privacy</h1>
<p class="muted">How @Model.ServiceName handles personal data, following the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
    The server is located in Germany.</p>

<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
<div class="panel">
    @if (Model.HasOperator)
    {
        <p><strong>@Model.Web.OperatorName</strong></p>
        @if (Model.Web.OperatorAddress.Length > 0)
        {
            <p>@Model.Web.OperatorAddress</p>
        }
        @if (Model.Web.OperatorContact.Length > 0)
        {
            <p>Contact: @Model.Web.OperatorContact</p>
        }
    }
    else
    {
        <p class="muted">The operator of this server has not entered their contact details yet (setting Web:OperatorName,
            Web:OperatorAddress, Web:OperatorContact).</p>
    }
</div>

<h2>What is stored, why and for how long</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose and legal basis</th><th>Kept</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>Account: user name, password hash (never the password itself), optional e-mail address, role, status,
                    a hash of your recovery code, profile visibility, creation and last login time</td>
                <td>Providing your account (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR)</td>
                <td>Until you delete the account</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Sessions: a hash of the session token, a device label (game version or browser), the IP address at
                    login, times</td>
                <td>Keeping you logged in, showing your active sessions (Art. 6(1)(b))</td>
                <td>Until 30 days after the session ended or expired</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Security log: logins, failed logins, account changes, uploads flagged by plausibility checks and staff
                    actions, each with the IP address. A failed login with a user name that belongs to no account keeps
                    only a keyed hash of the typed name, never the name itself</td>
                <td>Protecting accounts and the service against abuse (Art. 6(1)(f), legitimate interest)</td>
                <td>180 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Online character: the character you play online (as the game saves it), its last 20 revisions and
                    your online play time</td>
                <td>Online play; shown on your profile when it is public (Art. 6(1)(b))</td>
                <td>Until you reset the character or delete the account</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Cloud save: your private backup of the local save (latest and 5 older revisions)</td>
                <td>The backup you asked for; never shown to anyone else (Art. 6(1)(b))</td>
                <td>Until you delete it or the account</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Achievements, play statistics and best times</td>
                <td>Your profile when it is public; rarity percentages count them without names (Art. 6(1)(b))</td>
                <td>Until you delete the account</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Rooms: room name, who was a member and when</td>
                <td>Running rooms and checking that achievements happened in online play (Art. 6(1)(b))</td>
                <td>The room record stays; your membership rows go with your account</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Technical log files of the service (errors, room and relay events)</td>
                <td>Keeping the service running (Art. 6(1)(f))</td>
                <td>30 days</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>Game traffic between players runs through the relay of this server. It carries the game inputs of a session and is
    not stored.</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>The website sets two cookies that are technically necessary: one that keeps you logged in and one that protects
    forms against cross-site request forgery. There is no tracking, no analytics, no advertising and nothing is loaded
    from other servers (no external fonts or scripts).</p>

<h2>Who receives data</h2>
<p>Nobody. Data is not sold or shared. The hosting provider of the server processes it only on the operator's behalf.
    Your user name and, when your profile is public, your online character and achievements are visible to everyone on
    this website; room names and the host's user name are visible in the room list while a room is open.</p>

<h2>Automated checks</h2>
<p>Uploads of the online character are checked for plausibility. A failed check only marks the upload for the staff
    to look at; nothing is decided or banned automatically.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You have the right to access your data (Art. 15), to correct it (Art. 16), to have it deleted (Art. 17), to restrict
    its processing (Art. 18), to receive it in a portable format (Art. 20), and to object to processing based on
    legitimate interest (Art. 21). You can also complain to a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77), for
    example the one of your German federal state.</p>

<h2>Deleting your data</h2>
<p>You can delete your account at any time in your <a href="/account">account settings</a>, or ask the operator to do
    it. Deleting removes your online character, cloud save, achievements, statistics, best times, sessions and e-mail
    address at once. The account row stays only as an anonymous placeholder ("deleted_" and a number), and the
    security log keeps its entries without your IP address until they expire after 180 days (failed logins typed with
    your user name lose its hash and their IP address too). Database backups roll over
    within about two months.</p>

<p class="muted small">Last updated: 29 October 2026.</p>
